{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3276","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3276","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3276\",\"parent_revision\":\"1fc9dfbc859dab7833fe8c674a1a802f9858a8798761f85444deff93d1daa965\",\"root_revision\":\"1fc9dfbc859dab7833fe8c674a1a802f9858a8798761f85444deff93d1daa965\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`agents/contract-verification.md` line 151 states: \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \u2014 you register no artifact and write no task state.\\\" This assumes a synchronous dispatch model where the caller receives the subagent's final text as a direct return value.\\n\\nObserved during this session while running `/dh:implement-feature` on plan Pd95e593c for #3151: dispatching `dh:contract-verification` via the `Agent` tool returned only an async \\\"Spawned successfully\\\" acknowledgment. The agent completed its analysis and went idle twice (confirmed via `ListAgents`), but no message with actual content was ever delivered back \u2014 only bare `idle_notification` events with no `summary` field, unlike every other subagent dispatched in the same session (impact-analyst, fact-checker, classifier, rtica-assessor, alignment-analyst, groomer, feature-researcher, architect, swarm-task-planner, t0/t1 task agents), all of which reported back with a `summary` field containing real content. Sending the idle agent a direct follow-up question asking it to restate its verdict also produced no reply.\\n\\nThe `Agent` tool's own documentation states: \\\"Your plain text output is NOT visible to other agents \u2014 to communicate, you MUST call [SendMessage].\\\" That is the observed cause: `contract-verification.md`'s instructions never tell the agent to call `SendMessage`; they tell it to just \\\"output\\\" its finding as its response, consistent with a synchronous dispatch model this environment does not use for agent-tool dispatch.\\n\\nImpact: `implement-feature`'s Progress Loop step 4a (post-task contract verification) silently produces no usable result under this environment's async dispatch \u2014 the orchestrator either blocks indefinitely waiting for a message that never arrives, or gives up and has to verify the contract manually (as happened this session), defeating the point of delegating the check.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: this is the same class of gap already fixed for a sibling agent \u2014 `git log` shows a merged commit \\\"fix(development-harness): add SendMessage completion report to impact-analyst (#3249)\\\" that added exactly this kind of completion-report step to `dh:impact-analyst`. `dh:contract-verification` appears to have been missed by that same fix, and other `dh:*` agents dispatched by the same Progress Loop may share the identical gap \u2014 not verified for any agent besides contract-verification in this session.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: possible directions for grooming to evaluate, not requirements \u2014 (1) add an explicit `SendMessage` step to `contract-verification.md`'s Output Format section, mirroring whatever change PR #3249 made to `impact-analyst.md`; (2) audit the other `dh:*` agents invoked by `implement-feature`/`add-new-feature`'s Progress Loop for the same synchronous-response assumption, since any could have the identical gap and it would surface the same way (silent, not an error).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-28/29, while running /dh:implement-feature on plan Pd95e593c (#3151), dispatching dh:contract-verification for task T1\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"70c60782d4e45c100b8e57e91ba3bef05d69bb7a5c9d7babdc1e45200f768d0c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRRO79A\"}"}